#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for the gadget snap, including gadget.yaml, device "
"storage layouts, boot configuration, defaults, interfaces, and lifecycle "
"hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:8
msgid "The gadget snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:10
msgid ""
"The gadget snap is responsible for defining and configuring system "
"properties specific to one or more devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:12
msgid "The gadget metadata and content defines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:13
msgid "The layout of the volumes that comprise the device storage and image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:14
msgid ""
"Configuration for the bootloader to use. The gadget also ships the "
"bootloader itself and other boot assets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:15
msgid "Default configuration options to use when snaps are installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:16
msgid ""
"Interface connections configured in the `connections:` section are executed "
"on the device’s first boot only. Later changes to this section -- that is, "
"changes added to the device at run time through gadget refreshes -- are not "
"applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:17
msgid ""
"Optional hooks that are invoked to control and customise the behaviour over "
"the device lifecycle, e.g. installation, initialisation and establishing "
"device identity, factory reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:19
msgid ""
"See [Build a gadget snap](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/gadget-building) for "
"details on how a gadget snap can be built. For store deployment, gadget "
"snaps must be produced by the device {ref}`brand store <ref-glossary_brand-"
"store>`, as defined in the [model assertion](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/"
"reference/assertions/model), or a reference gadget must be used. It is "
"perfectly possible for different models to share a gadget snap."
msgstr ""

