msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:81
msgid "Ubuntu Core typically uses the following storage partitions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:83
msgid ""
"**ubuntu-seed** (role: system-seed; *read-only, ext4 or typically vfat*)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:84
msgid "**ubuntu-boot** (role: system-boot; *read-only, ext4* or *vfat*):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:85
msgid "**ubuntu-save** (role: system-save; *writable, ext4*, **encrypted**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:86
msgid "**ubuntu-data** (role: system-data; *writable*, ext4, **encrypted**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:88
msgid ""
"**ubuntu-save** is mandatory on an encrypted system. The *initramfs* "
"bootstrapped from **ubuntu-boot** is responsible for decrypting both the "
"**ubuntu-save** and **ubuntu-data** partitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:90
msgid ""
"**ubuntu-data** needs to be the last partition. No extra partitions can be "
"inserted between **ubuntu-boot**, **ubuntu-save** and **ubuntu-data**. If "
"extra partitions are required, they need to be declared and created before "
"**ubuntu-boot**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:92
msgid ""
"The structure section lists entities with gadget data inside the image, most "
"of which are partitions with a file system inside, with the exception of "
"structures of type: bare, which can describe a region of data without a "
"corresponding entry in the partition table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:94
msgid "Dynamic kernel parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:96
msgid ""
"There are two {ref}`system options <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-set-system-"
"options>` that can be used to add new kernel boot parameters to a system "
"that has been deployed and is running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:98
msgid ""
"{ref}`system.kernel.cmdline-append <reference-administration-system-options-"
"kernel-cmdline-append>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:99
msgid ""
"{ref}`system.kernel.dangerous-cmdline-append <reference-administration-"
"system-options-kernel-dangerous-cmdline-append>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:101
msgid ""
"The second setting can be run (dangerously) without any prior configuration, "
"but the first setting will permit **only** boot parameters verified against "
"an *allow list* defined within the gadget snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:103
msgid ""
"The _allow list_ defines both parameters and their possible arguments, and "
"takes takes following format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:105
#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:118
msgid ""
"kernel-cmdline:\n"
"    allow:\n"
"        - kernel-parameter-1=1\n"
"        - kernel-parameter-2=*\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:112
msgid ""
"The `*` character can be used as a wildcard to accept any parameter "
"argument. It can not be used to limit an argument's scope. For example, "
"`kernel-parameter-2=*` is acceptable, but `kernel-parameter-2=a*` is not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:114
msgid ""
"See [Modifying kernel boot parameters](https://ubuntu.com/core/docs/kernel-"
"options) for more details on defining kernel boot parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:116
msgid "Static kernel parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:124
msgid "To which we should add"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:125
msgid ""
"    append:\n"
"         - kernel-parameters-3=value\n"
"     remove:\n"
"         - console=ttyS0\n"
"         - panic=*\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-gadget-snap.md:133
msgid ""
"The parameters from `append` will be added to the default command line. The "
